 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.4 (2026-11-01)
+
+- Reject a DHCPv6 Reply carrying a Client Identifier when the request was
+  anonymous, as required by [RFC 8415 section 16.10](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8415.html#section-16.10).
+  Previously that Reply could install another client's DNS servers and end
+  the exchange before a valid anonymous Reply arrived.
+- Preserve matching identifiers and the existing tolerance for identified
+  clients receiving a Reply without a Client Identifier. No public API or
+  dependency changes.
+
 ## 0.4.3 (2026-10-31)
 
 - Bound each DHCPv6 client's pending datagrams to a 64-entry FIFO. Excess
